= Specification and design

- Describe what your project does (Specification).
  - Define the user requirements of your project.
  - Include use cases to explain how users will interact with the system.
- Provide details on how it does so (Design)
  - Discuss the different design choices and then provide justification for the
    design that you have chosen. Use design schematics (if needed).
  - Provide details of the system such as the architectural overview, user
    interface, data flows, important algorithms etc.
  - You are highly encouraged to make use of diagrams such as UML diagrams,
    state transition diagrams, block diagrams (illustrating the different
    modules of your system) in this section.
